      <title outputclass="chapter_sub-titles">What Is Artificial Intelligence?</title>
      <p>The advantages of using <tm tmtype="tm" trademark="DB2 Universal Database"> <tm tmclass="ibm" tmtype="reg" trademark="DB2">DB2</tm> Universal Database</tm> are well known.</p>
      <p>Artificial Intelligence (AI) refers to the simulation of human intelligence in machines that are programmed to think, learn, and problem-solve. AI encompasses a variety of subfields, including machine learning, deep learning, natural language processing, and computer vision.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <title outputclass="chapter_sub-titles">Overview of AI Technologies</title>
      <p><b>Machine Learning (ML):</b> A subset of AI where algorithms enable machines to learn from data without explicit programming. It's widely used for tasks like prediction, classification, and pattern recognition.</p>
      <p><b>Deep Learning:</b> A more advanced subset of machine learning involving neural networks with many layers. Deep learning is crucial for complex tasks like image recognition and autonomous driving.</p>
      <p><b>Natural Language Processing (NLP):</b> This enables machines to understand, interpret, and generate human language, enabling voice assistants, chatbots, and language translation systems.</p>
      <p><b>Computer Vision:</b> A field within AI that enables computers to interpret and understand visual data, used in applications such as facial recognition and autonomous vehicles.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <title outputclass="chapter_sub-titles">How AI Systems Work</title>
      <p>AI systems function by analyzing vast amounts of data and using algorithms to recognize patterns, make decisions, and improve their performance over time. This enables automation of complex tasks, optimizing efficiency across various industries.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <title outputclass="chapter_sub-titles">Key Components of AI Systems</title>
      <p>AI systems rely on several key components to function: data sets, algorithms, computational power, and neural networks.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <title outputclass="chapter_sub-titles">Data Sets</title>
      <p>Data sets are crucial in training AI models. High-quality, large-scale data sets allow AI systems to learn from real-world examples, making them more accurate and reliable in their predictions and decisions.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <title outputclass="chapter_sub-titles">Algorithms and Computational Power</title>
      <p>Algorithms are the backbone of AI, enabling machines to learn patterns and perform tasks. The computational power provided by high-performance processors accelerates the processing of complex algorithms, allowing for real-time decision-making.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <title outputclass="chapter_sub-titles">Advantages and Challenges of AI</title>
      <p>AI offers numerous benefits, such as increased efficiency, reduced human error, and the ability to handle large-scale tasks autonomously. However, challenges remain, including ethical concerns, data privacy, and the need for skilled professionals to manage AI systems.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <title outputclass="chapter_sub-titles">Environmental and Economic Benefits</title>
      <p>AI can optimize energy consumption, improve resource allocation, and reduce waste in industries, contributing to environmental sustainability. Economically, AI creates new opportunities, automates processes, and can drive growth across various sectors.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <title outputclass="chapter_sub-titles">Barriers to Widespread Adoption</title>
      <p>Key barriers to AI adoption include the high costs of technology, the shortage of AI talent, and concerns about job displacement. Despite these barriers, AI is becoming increasingly integrated into industries like healthcare, finance, and manufacturing, driving innovation and progress.</p>
    </section>
